## Backend

The bound pack's `backend.mdc` and `pack.json` name the stack, layers, auth marker, and migration tool. Pack `java` is Java 21, Spring Boot, Spring Security, Flyway, and ArchUnit. Do not copy that stack into another pack.

## BFF (Backend-for-Frontend)

The BFF uses the same pack as the backend. Its implement skill is `implement-bff`.

| Area | Mandatory |
|------|-----------|
| Role | Aggregation, UI DTOs, auth/session edge, GET cache, rate limit, unified errors |
| Clients | Timeout, retry, and breaker on outbound calls; `X-Correlation-ID`; service auth |
| Pipeline | Auth → rate limit → cache (GET) / invalidation (writes) → validation → handler |
| Rules | Thin BFF; domain logic in backend services; version the BFF API independently |

## Frontend

The UI is the bound pack's `ui` id. Read that UI pack's `layout`, `verify`, and `coverage`. The React example is `core/ui/react` and `frontend-web.mdc`.

## Integration and composition

| Area | Mandatory |
|------|-----------|
| Principles | DB per service; OpenAPI-first; REST + events |
| Per service | `/health`, `/ready`, `/live`; Prometheus; OpenAPI; JWT + S2S auth; tracing |
| Headers | `Authorization`, `X-API-Key` (S2S), `X-Correlation-ID` |
| Events | `order.created`-style names; idempotent consumers; DLQ + retry |
| Resilience | Breaker, exponential retry, timeout outbound; BFF may aggregate in parallel |

HTTP detail: `api-and-events.mdc`. Observability defaults: `project-delivery-core.mdc`.

## OMS domain (reference — when relevant)

| Area | Mandatory |
|------|-----------|
| Style | Event-driven; DB per service; sagas; idempotency keys on writes |
| Contexts | Order, Inventory, Payment, Fulfillment, order ops |
| Orders | `POST /api/v1/orders` with idempotency_key, customer_id, channel, items, addresses; bulk → `202` + `batch_id` |
| Events | `ORDER_CREATED`, `ORDER_VALIDATED`, `ORDER_CONFIRMED`, `ORDER_CANCELLED`, `ORDER_COMPLETED` |
| Data | Optimistic locking; status history; saga compensations |

